// SA — the Shahada ("There is no god but God; Muhammad is the Messenger
// of God") in white Thuluth calligraphy above a white sword, on a green
// field. Given the religious significance of this text, hand-approximating
// the calligraphy was never attempted — the exact official reference
// construction used on Wikipedia/Wikimedia Commons
// (File:Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg) was downloaded directly via curl and
// its calligraphy and sword group re-serialized with Python's
// xml.etree.ElementTree, then embedded verbatim via
// dangerouslySetInnerHTML — every stroke of the Shahada and the sword's
// exact silhouette reproduced as in the source, not redrawn. The source
// file's own coordinate system and scale(.375) transform are used
// directly (source viewBox already matches this project's 900x600
